<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Telmex raised to buy.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Telmex raised to buy.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Mexican brokerage Abaco upgraded Mexican telephone firm Telefonos de Mexico (Telmex) to buy from buy long-term.</p>
<p>-- Analysts Claudia Gonzales and Alexander Anderson also raised their 1997 earnings estimates on the company to $3.72 per ADR. The report did not say what its original 1997 earnings estimate was.</p>
<p>-- The analysts said Telmex stock has reacted well to news of recent tariff re-balancing, and non-competitive long-distance rates by its rivals.</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom, +525 728-9565))</p>
</text>
